text.section:
The Department may issue a temporary registration to a fleet logistics provider if:

Application for temporary registration is made by the fleet logistics provider acting as duly authorized attorney-in-fact for the title owner;


The fleet logistics provider is registered to conduct business in Virginia;


The fleet logistics provider has or will have custody and control of the vehicle at the time the temporary registration becomes effective;


The fleet logistics provider or title owner has submitted to the appropriate authority the information necessary to title or register the vehicle in the Commonwealth or another state prior to the expiration of the temporary registration and the vehicle was not temporarily registered during the period immediately preceding the application for temporary registration;


The title owner prior to the temporary registration will remain the title owner when the vehicle is titled and registered in the Commonwealth or another state;


The vehicle is an insured motor vehicle as defined in § 46.2-705;


The fleet logistics provider has entered into an agreement with the Department to use the print-on-demand program described in this section; and


The fleet logistics provider has paid applicable fees for the temporary registration authorized by this section.
